R"VG(
# industrial6.vg (H-04; the second pass 2026-10-10): a voice on a wax cylinder (the industrial age) or a disc (the modern): someone of
# the history speaking into the machine at home, about themselves, their house and their town, the season, what they ate, what they
# believe, the news of the year (the letter's register), and whoever will hear it. Each line its own (`once`), drawn from pools of the
# people's own things.

genre.voice (words=31..140)
  {@cast writer}{voice.open} {voice.body} {voice.close}

voice.open (formula)
  This is {$me:name}, speaking at {$me.home}, the {#year:ord} year of {city}.
  Can you hear me? This is {$me:name}. They say this machine will keep my voice.
  Testing. This is {$me:name}, {$me.trade}, at {$me.home}.
  Is it going? It is going. My name is {$me:name}.
  {$me:name} speaking. The man says to talk as if to a friend, so: hello, friend.
  (medium=disc) This record was made at {$me.home} by {$me:name}, for the family.

voice.body
  {voice.line} {voice.line} {voice.line}
  {voice.line} {voice.line} {@news public letter}
  {voice.line} {@news public letter} {voice.line} {voice.line}
  {voice.line} {voice.line} {voice.line} {voice.line}

voice.line
  (once 2) {voice.about} {voice.tail}
  (once) {voice.machine}
  (once has:$child) {voice.child}
  (once) {voice.season}
  (once) {voice.town}
  (once) {voice.work}
  (once) {voice.table}
  (once) {voice.faith}
  (once) {voice.house}
  (once) {voice.song}
  (once) {voice.future}
  (once) {voice.beast}
  (once has:$spouse) {voice.spouse}
  (once) {voice.happy}
  (once stage>=1) I do not know who will hear this, {voice.hear}. I hope it is someone who knows what {crop} is.

voice.about
  We live at {$me.home}, by the {voice.place},
  I have been a {$me.trade} for {#$me.age:about|year},
  (has:$spouse) {$spouse:full} is in the next room,
  The {crop} is in and the evenings are long,
  My father would not have believed in this machine,
  We are having {festival} next week,
  (has:$me.home.ptrade) {$me.home} lives by {$me.home.ptrade}, as it always has,
  I was born the year the {voice.born} came,
  There are {n} of us in this house,
voice.tail
  and that is all you need to know about us.
  and I would not change it.
  which is more than most can say.
  and I have nothing to complain of, much.
  and I thought someone should hear what we sounded like.
  and the {bird} are loud tonight, if you can hear them.
  and I am too old to pretend otherwise.
voice.place
  river
  station
  old market
  mill
  square
  north road
voice.born
  (inv.railway=1) railway
  big flood
  new bridge
  comet
  sickness
  long winter

voice.machine
  I am speaking into a [horn|brass funnel|machine], which is a strange thing to do at my age, and stranger after {drink}.
  If you are hearing this, the machine works, and the man who sold it to us for {n} {coin} was not lying.
  The machine cost {n} {coin}, and my {voice.critic} says we should have bought {voice.instead} instead.
  I keep wanting to stop and let the machine answer, the way you wait for the {beast} to answer.
  They say this will last longer than I will. I hope it is kinder to my voice than the {voice.mirror} is to my face.
voice.instead
  a {beast}
  {n} {herd}
  a new {garment.n}
  a winter's {fuel}
voice.mirror
  mirror
  water in the {watersrc.n}
  glass in the shop window
voice.critic
  wife
  husband
  sister
  brother
  mother
  neighbour

voice.child
  My {$child.kin} {$child:name} is here, and will say something. No? No.
  {$child:name} wants to sing, so {$child:name} will sing later, when I have finished.
  {$child:name} is hiding under the table and laughing, so if you hear laughing, that is the reason.

voice.spouse
  {$spouse:name} says I am to say that the {crop2} came up well this year.
  {$spouse:name} is listening and pretending not to.

voice.season
  It is {season.now}. {weather.now} is at the windows, and the {herd} are complaining about it.
  Outside it is {weather.now}, and the {herd} are in, and so am I.
  It is {season.now}, and the light goes early now; we light the lamps at {voice.lamp}.
  We have had {weather.now} for a week, and the children are wild with it, and the {beast} wilder.
voice.lamp
  the noon meal
  the {nth} bell
  dusk, as everyone does

voice.town
  The town is bigger than when I was a child, and [louder|dirtier|kinder, in its way]; there were {herd} in {streets.of} then.
  (has:$me.home.landmark) From this window I can see {$me.home.landmark}; I have looked at it all my life.
  (has:$me.home.quarter) We are in {$me.home.quarter}, where the streets are narrow and everyone knows your business.
  (inv.railway=1) The train goes past at the bottom of the garden; you can hear it now, if you listen, over the {bird}.
  They have put lamps in {streets.of}, and the young ones are out half the night at the {ind.sport}.
  The {craft} works whistle at six, and the whole street gets up.

voice.work
  We say in the {craft} trade that {proverb}.
  My hands smell of {voice.smell} and always will.
  The work at the {craft} works is hard and the pay is {n} {coin} a week, and we are glad of it.
  I learned my trade from my mother, who learned it from hers, and nobody has improved it.
voice.smell
  {fuel}
  the dye vats
  {crop}
  oil

voice.table
  We had {food} tonight, and {drink}, because it is {festival} soon.
  Supper was {food}, as it is most nights, and nobody complained, much.
  We have {drink} on the table and I have had some, so forgive me.

voice.faith
  Last {festival} we {rite.do}, as we always have, and ate {food} after.
  We keep the old ways in this house: we {ind.rite.v}.
  (faith!=philosophy faith!=machine) I want to say a word for {god}, who has been good to us, mostly, and to the {herd}, always.
ind.rite.v
  light the lamp at dusk with {fuel}
  say the names of the dead at {festival}
  give the first cup of {drink} to the ground
  keep the rest day quiet, even the {beast}
  hang {colour.holy} cloth on the door at the new year

voice.house
  We live in {house.one}, with {roofs} that leak in {season.any}.
  The house is old; my grandfather built it of {walls.of}, and my grandmother told him how.
  There is a {colour.any} door on our house, with {motif.over} over it, so you will know it if you come.

voice.song
  Here is a bit of the {voice.songkind} they sing at {festival}. No, I will not sing it; {voice.nosing}. Well, a little.
  My mother used to sing to me about {river}; I have forgotten the words, but not the tune, which went with {instrument}.
  Listen: that is {instrument}, next door. They practise every evening, and the {beast} howls.

voice.future
  If you are hearing this a long time from now, I hope the {crop} still grows where you are.
  To whoever is listening: we were ordinary people, and we ate {food} and drank {drink} and had a good time.
  I wonder what you eat, whoever you are, and whether you have {fruit}. Here it is {food}, mostly.
  If this lasts, tell them about us at {$me.home}; we were here, and we kept {herd} and grew {crop}.

voice.happy
  I want to say that we were happy here, [mostly|on the whole|more than we said at the time], in spite of {voice.trouble}.
  We were happy in this house, {voice.whowith}.
voice.trouble
  {weather}
  the {pest}
  the neighbours
  the price of {crop}
voice.whowith
  the {herd} and the children and the rest of us
  most of the time
  which is more than the neighbours were
voice.beast
  The {beast} is asleep by the stove and will not say anything.
  That noise is our {beast}. It wants its dinner. It always wants its dinner.

voice.close (formula)
  That is all. Turn it off. How do you turn it off?
  Goodbye. This was {$me:name}.
  There. It is done.
  That is enough. Is it still going? Stop it now.
  {god.keep}. Goodbye.
voice.songkind
  song
  lullaby
  marching song
  {craft} song
  harvest song
voice.nosing
  the {beast} would join in
  my voice is not what it was
  you would not thank me
  the neighbours are listening
voice.hear
  or when
  the way things are going
  now that the {craft} works are closed
  with half the street gone
)VG"
